---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const site = Astro.site ?? new URL('https://usdtoworld.com');
const breadcrumbSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: site.toString() },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Disclaimer', item: new URL('/disclaimer', site).toString() },
  ],
};
---
<Layout
  title="Disclaimer | UsdtoWorld"
  description="UsdtoWorld's exchange rate data is provided for informational purposes only. Read our full disclaimer before making financial decisions."
  path="/disclaimer"
  schema={[breadcrumbSchema]}
>
  <div class="container page-hero">
    <Breadcrumbs trail={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Disclaimer', href: '/disclaimer' }]} />
  </div>
  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="container prose">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1>Disclaimer</h1>
      <p class="updated-note">Last updated: October 3, 2026</p>

      <div class="plain-summary">
        <strong>In plain terms:</strong> the rates on this site are for information only, not financial
        advice. We're not a bank or money transfer service, so use a licensed provider for an actual
        transfer. Rates can lag the real market by a few seconds, so treat them as a close estimate rather
        than a guaranteed number.
      </div>

      <h2>Informational purposes only</h2>
      <p>
        The exchange rates, conversions, charts, worked examples and currency commentary displayed on UsdtoWorld
        are provided for general informational purposes only. They do not constitute financial, investment, tax,
        or legal advice, and should not be relied upon as the sole basis for any financial decision. Consult a
        qualified professional about your own circumstances.
      </p>

      <h2>No guarantee of accuracy</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to display accurate, up-to-date exchange rates sourced from a third-party market data provider, but
        rates can change within seconds and figures shown may lag real-time market conditions. When the live
        feed cannot be reached, the converter may display your last saved rate, which will be older. We make no
        warranty, express or implied, regarding the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of any rate or conversion.
      </p>

      <h2>Mid-market rates are not the rate you will receive</h2>
      <p>
        The rate shown is a mid-market reference, the midpoint between wholesale buy and sell prices. Banks,
        money changers, card networks and transfer apps add margins and fees, so the amount you actually pay or
        receive will usually be less favourable. For thinly traded currencies the gap can be large. Always compare
        the total cost and the total amount received from your provider.
      </p>

      <h2>Dated snapshots and historical commentary</h2>
      <p>
        Conversion tables on guide pages are snapshots labelled with the date they were taken and are approximate.
        Historical ranges, trend descriptions and explanations of what moves a currency are general background, not
        forecasts. Nobody can reliably predict exchange rates, and nothing on this Site should be read as a
        prediction or a recommendation to buy, sell or send money at a particular time.
      </p>

      <h2>Not for accounting, tax or contractual use</h2>
      <p>
        UsdtoWorld rates are not official reference rates. If you need a rate for invoicing, bookkeeping, a tax
        return, customs valuation or a contract, use the rate your contract, accountant or the relevant authority
        specifies, such as a central bank's published reference rate for a given date. Our figures can help you
        estimate and plan, but they should not be cited as the legally or contractually correct rate.
      </p>

      <h2>Not a financial institution</h2>
      <p>
        UsdtoWorld is not a bank, money transmitter, broker, or financial institution. We do not execute
        currency trades, hold funds, or facilitate transfers. Any actual currency exchange or transfer should
        be conducted through a licensed bank, authorised dealer or money transfer service, whose quoted
        rates and fees may differ from figures shown here.
      </p>

      <h2>Laws, sanctions and restrictions</h2>
      <p>
        Rules on moving money across borders differ by country and change over time. Limits, documentation
        requirements, sanctions and capital controls can affect whether and how a payment is possible, particularly for
        some currencies and routes. Information on this Site about such rules is general and may be out of date, so
        confirm the current position with your bank or the relevant regulator before you act.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising and third-party links</h2>
      <p>
        This site displays advertising and may link to third-party services or resources. Advertisements are
        supplied by Google AdSense and are not endorsements, and our guides are written independently of them. We are
        not responsible for the content, accuracy, or practices of any third-party site or advertiser.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, UsdtoWorld shall not be liable for any
        loss or damage arising from reliance on information provided on this site, including any financial
        loss resulting from currency conversion decisions.
      </p>

      <h2>Errors and corrections</h2>
      <p>
        If you believe a rate, figure or statement on the Site is wrong, please tell us through the
        <a href="/contact">Contact page</a> with the page address and what looks incorrect. We review every report and
        correct confirmed errors on the live page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
